From ccf56184adda2c7bc6133a854f647dbe173a08f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wolfram Sang <wsa+renesas@sang-engineering.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:11:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 0398/2868] dmaengine: sh: rz-dmac: add r7s72100 support

commit 32172b3e3265833a367e41842fa8b7eaa0acae96 upstream.

This SoC needs to make getting resets optional. Descriptions are
reworded to be more generic.

Signed-off-by: Wolfram Sang <wsa+renesas@sang-engineering.com>
Reviewed-by: Philipp Zabel <p.zabel@pengutronix.de>
Reviewed-by: Geert Uytterhoeven <geert+renesas@glider.be>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20241007110200.43166-8-wsa+renesas@sang-engineering.com
Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul <vkoul@kernel.org>
[PL: dropped kconfig changes]
Signed-off-by: Lad Prabhakar <prabhakar.mahadev-lad.rj@bp.renesas.com>
Signed-off-by: Nobuhiro Iwamatsu <nobuhiro.iwamatsu.x90@mail.toshiba>
Reviewed-by: Pavel Machek <pavel@nabladev.com>
---
 drivers/dma/sh/rz-dmac.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/sh/rz-dmac.c b/drivers/dma/sh/rz-dmac.c
index 652b0f51d9e9..cfa6aca26ed2 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/sh/rz-dmac.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/sh/rz-dmac.c
@@ -953,7 +953,7 @@ static int rz_dmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	/* Initialize the channels. */
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&dmac->engine.channels);
 
-	dmac->rstc = devm_reset_control_array_get_exclusive(&pdev->dev);
+	dmac->rstc = devm_reset_control_array_get_optional_exclusive(&pdev->dev);
 	if (IS_ERR(dmac->rstc))
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(dmac->rstc),
 				     "failed to get resets\n");
